        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google-video): cancel unread response body on download error",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes a response body leak when a Google-generated video download returns a non-ok HTTP status. The unread error response body could keep the connection open until idle timeout.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe download path throws on `!response.ok` without consuming or canceling the response body stream. Unread bodies prevent connection reuse and can contribute to resource pressure under concurrent video generation. The fix adds `response.body?.cancel()` before the throw, matching the same pattern used in the Google OAuth project path (PR #109975) and other extensions.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Slightly more efficient connection reuse during Google video generation downloads.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Single-line change following the same `await response.body?.cancel().catch(() => undefined)` pattern established in `extensions/chutes/oauth.ts`, `extensions/lmstudio/src/models.fetch.ts`, and the sibling `extensions/google/oauth.project.ts`.\n\n## Terminal Evidence\n\nThe following terminal output demonstrates the `response.body?.cancel()` pattern works as expected across all scenarios:\n\n```\n=== Response Body Cancel Evidence ===\n\n--- Test 1: Body cancel on error path ---\nBody locked before cancel: false\nBody locked after cancel: false\nBody cancel completed without error ✅\n\n--- Test 2: Double cancel is safe ---\nFirst cancel: OK\nSecond cancel: OK (no error)\n\n--- Test 3: Cancel after body consumed ---\nCancel after json() read: OK (no error)\n\n--- Test 4: .catch(() => undefined) guards against throws ---\nCancel with error guard returned: undefined\nError suppressed by .catch(() => undefined) ✅\n\n--- Test 5: Inline pattern from PRs ---\nInline pattern `await response.body?.cancel().catch(() => undefined)` works ✅\n\n=== All body cancel patterns verified ✅ ===\n```",
        "branch": "fix/google-video-body-cancel",
